# Story: someone who never touches the keyboard arranges windows by dragging.
# The simulated display is 1440x900 with a 25-point menu bar.
# Reference: T01 T02 T11 T17.
# The three tiling switches of the guide's section 2 are off: with macOS's own tiling on, the left, right and top edges of the screen are macOS's (Q23).
# As the first build shipped it: a docked window is dragged out onto the Desktop beside another.
set desktopColumn true
mac-tiling off
open Safari
open Notes
# Drag Safari to the left screen edge: it docks.
drag 101 3 450 cmd
expect docked 101
# Drop Notes near Safari's right edge: it docks beside Safari.
drag 102 700 450 cmd
expect docked 102
expect left-of 101 102
# Drag Safari out onto the Desktop: it floats again and Notes takes its space.
drag 101 1300 450 cmd
expect floating 101
expect docked 102
expect count docked 1
